oxynol  is also known as vamatoxin  that causes problems in many wheat-based  products  and we really want to avoid  these mycotoxins getting into any part  of the food chain  now we will go over mycotoxin chemical  structures  shown here are the structures for  fumonosyn b1  b2  b3 and ochrotoxin a  fumonosins which were discovered in 1988  in south africa  differentiate by a hydroxyl group  fumonosines  predominantly occur in cereal grains  especially in maize  mechanistic studies suggest disruption  of lipid metabolism as being the mode of  action for fumonosyn b1 mediated  toxicity  fumonosin b1 is not mutagenic but is  capable of introducing reactive oxygen  species that could lead to dna damage  fumonosin b1 caused effects in some  developmental and reproductive studies  a slight  significant impact of ocratoxin is that  it occurs in such a wide variety of  commodities such as raisins barley soy  products and coffee  in amounts that may be relatively low  however significant amounts may  accumulate in the blood and other  tissues  because it derives from potential  different sources  ochrodoxin produces necrosis of the  proximal  tubular  epithelium and then is released whereby  it is reabsorbed by albumin and  continues to circulate via the  bloodstream  okra toxin is a carcinogen in rats and  mice  and it is suspect agent of a human  disease named balkan endemic  nephropathy  that affects the kidneys which tumors  are often associated  other mycotoxin chemical structures are  shown here including t2 toxin  ht2 toxin deoxy navalnol navalnol  and xarellanone  t2 and ht2 toxins are members of the  fungal metabolites known as  trichrothesenes  corn wheat barley oats rice rye and  other crops have been reported to  contain the t2 toxin  the major attribute of the t2 toxin and  other trichotins is that they inhibit  protein synthesis  which is followed by a secondary  disruption of dna and rna synthesis  it can decrease antibody levels  immunoglobulins and certain other  humoral factors  the effects include weight loss or poor  weight gain  bloody  necrosis or beak lesions and  hemorrhaging  t2 results from an esterification of the  hydroxyl group of ht2 with acetic acid  nib  and dawn known as navalny and  deoxynebolanol  differentiate between each other by the  presence of a hydroxyl group  in the volanol  deoxynol is also known as vomitoxin  xorellanone is chemically a phenolic  resoric  acid lactone in fact it is often present  in combination with the oxynovalanol  the compound is mostly found in corn  however it is found also in other  important crops such as wheat  barley sorghum and rye  zarellanone is the primary toxin causing  infertility  abortion or other breeding problems in  mammals  lastly we have the mycotoxin chemical  structures for aflatoxins listed below  as you can see aflatoxin b1 b2 g1 g2 m1  and m2 which is the primary focus of the  immunoaffinity column that i will be  discussing today  aflatoxins are produced by two species  of the genus  aspergillus  aspergillus flavus and aspergillus  parasiticus  aflatoxins are  genotoxic and carcinogenic and can cause  both acute and chronic toxicity in  humans  aflatoxin b1 and b2  differ for a double bond and the same is  true for aflatoxin g1 and g2 along with  m1 and m2  corn cottonseed peanuts and tree nuts  are main crops affected the presence  innate fluorescent properties aflatoxin  is the most carcinogenic naturally  occurring substance known to man  in summary mycotoxins are health  hazard-causing compounds  and it is not a case  that they have been ranked as the most  important chronic dietary risk factor  higher than  synthetic contaminants plant toxins food  additives or pesticide residues  one very interesting thing about  mycotoxins is that they are not  ubiquinous  you know you may find the mold in your  commodity wherever it may be and not the  toxin or vice versa  the mold may have been eliminated but  the mycotoxin while you can't see it is  still there  so why is that  well different ecological parameters or  stressors affect mycotoxin production  by the differential fungal species  mentioned earlier  and those include moisture  spore load  the temperature of the environment  if there's any other bugs that have  infected the plant  or the storage area  what substrate they are growing on  oxidization levels  how long something has been stored  maybe some mechanical damage that  occurred during harvest  or insect damage and one important note  is that organic crops or crops that have  not been treated with fungicides are  especially vulnerable  to contamination by mycotoxins  so there are many strategies to growers  and producers  that they can use to minimize risks to  the crops and the products  for example not growers can reduce the  percentage of early split nuts by  irrigation management  and avoiding tree stress  early harvest also cuts down on  naval orange worm damage  using a rod stock that minimizes early  split nuts and carefully  use  dormancy breaking chemicals can also  prevent early splits  processors can reduce aflatoxin levels  by drying nuts as soon as possible after  arrival  sorting can remove contaminated in-shell  nuts based on the shell discoloration  shell size and presence of insect frass  storage at proper moisture levels and  avoiding post-harvest rehydration will  also prevent contamination  as we have discussed aflatoxins are  carcinogenic mycotoxins that have  adverse health effects on both humans  and animals  consuming contaminated food and feed  a method has been developed for the  highly sensitive and selective  determination of regulated aflatoxins  in a wide range of commodities  the extraction of aflatoxins from  representative commodities of interest  corn wheat oats red chili  black pepper  cocoa and a traditional chinese medicine  was performed using a solvent extraction  then immunoaffinity column cleanup on  the new aflatest wb sr plus  immunoaffinity column  chromatographic separation was  demonstrated using both the waters hplc  alliance and the waters uplc acuity  h-class plus platforms using  fluorescence detection  supported with post-column  derivatization and large flow cell  respectively the performance of the  method was evaluated through replicate  analysis of spiked test portions  of seven different matrices  overall recovery was shown to be  excellent between 92 and 116  with relative standard deviations lower  than 8 percent  the method was found to be specific as  no interference peaks were observed for  blank samples  the method has been demonstrated as  suitable for monitoring compliance with  regulatory limits set for aflatoxins in  food commodities globally  we have discussed mycotoxins in detail  and why we need to test for aflatoxins  in our food supply  our variety of testing solutions exist  for the determination of alpha toxins  ranging from easy to use rapid tests  which can be which can be used at the  point of production  to lab-based reference methods that are  more time-consuming but can be used to  provide a more comprehensive view of the  level of contamination  determination of actual toxins is a  challenging task due to the complexity  of the matrix  often with high lipid content  the low concentrations in which these  compounds are usually present and the  strict low regulatory limits  the combination of  cleaning up  using amino affinity columns based on  antibodies and analysis by hplc with  fluorescence  has been a prerequisite step to achieve  the desired sensitivity and selectivity  and has been successfully used as a  cost-effecting way to check compliance  with the regulatory limits for  aflatoxins for many years  vicam launched a new product  the aflatest wbsr plus immunoaffinity  column which can endure a high  concentration of organic solvent  while maintaining excellent recoveries  the objective of this study was to  examine the performance of using vicam's  aflatest wbsr plus immunoaffinity  columns with two separate hplc upoc  platforms  in both grains  corn wheat notes and difficult food  matrices such as spices chili powder and  black pepper  along with cocoa and a traditional  chinese medicine  using a standardized testing procedure  in addition to the aflatest wbsr plus  immunoaffinity column  it was evaluated for its ability to bind  steromycetin  which is another potent liver carcinogen  and a precursor to aflatoxin  in the results shown here  different concentrations of acetonitrile  are passed over the column at different  spiking levels  this chart shows acetonitrile effect on  afla test wbsr plus  recoveries  and as you can see in this for the two  nanogram mix and the 500 nanogram mix  there are very excellent recoveries  along with  great  percent cvs  the afflicate wbsr plus column was also  compared with our competitors columns  using increased solvent tolerance  we saw that aflates wbsr plus can  tolerate up to 40 percent methanol and  30 acetonitrile over the columns  this is based on 100 nanogram total  aflatoxin spiked into 20 percent of  cedar nitrile and a pbs solution  as shown here you can see that g2  recovery was  very good for the aflatest wb sr plus  column and the competitors had low g2  recoveries along with one competitor  that had a low aflatoxin b2  recovery shown here is the linearity and  lod and loq for spiked corn samples  as you can see the lod and loq are  within  regulatory limits for both the united  states and the eu and the linearity  showed recoveries  for the two nanogram to 500 nanogram  from 96  to 100  along with linearity of an r squared of  0.999  which is excellent  as mentioned previously  the aflatest  wbsr plus immunoaffinity column is also  capable of capturing the precursor to  aflatoxin stc  the scc recoveries in spiked corn  samples are shown here  the structure is also shown  next to the peak in the uplc  chromatogram from the analysis of an  extract of corn spiked with  25 micrograms per kilogram of stc  the recoveries ranged  in levels spiked from 4 to 50 micrograms  per kilogram from 92 percent to 98  percent and the cvs also were below  eight percent which is a very good for  this analysis  shown here is naturally contaminated  corn using a 90 acetonitrile extraction  and an 80  methanol extraction and in comparison  you can see for the higher level  naturally contaminated corn  the trilogy result that we had received  was 301 parts per billion and when we  ran this using our extraction  we received a 301.3  ppb results  with the methanol extraction you can see  that it was a bit lower for  the result compared to trilogy's result  which was  280 in comparison to the 301 ppb  this shows that higher levels of organic  extraction clearly  extract  aflatoxin out better and also with our  column being able to tolerate the higher  solvent it makes for an overall better  extraction with immunofinity cleanup  so one method was used for a complex  sample matrices analysis  10 grams of sample was weighed out  and  100 ml of 90 of senior nitrile water was  added to that into a blender and blended  for three minutes it was then filtered  ten mils was diluted with thirty mils of  two percent tween pbs  ten mils is passed over the afla test  wbsr plus immunoaffinity column  the column was then washed with  two times  of 10 ml of water  and it was eluded  with acetonitrile methanol at a one to  two ratio  the extract was then diluted and  injected onto the hplc or uplc  shown here are the results for wheat  oats cocoa black pepper and chili powder  in respect to their spiking levels  aoac recommended recoveries were 40 to  120 for the lower levels and 60 to 115  for the higher levels in which we fell  into the recommended range  for all of our  matrices using this method coupled with  the new immunoaffinity column  traditional chinese medicine was also  extracted using this method and the menu  column the afla test wbsr plus amino  affinity column  and the fallopia multiflora results are  shown below  spiked at 5  micrograms per kilogram and 20  micrograms per kilogram the aoc's  recommended recoveries are  75 to 120 for the 5 microgram  and 70 to 125 for the 20 microgram per  kilogram the rsds were all in range and  the recoveries were all in range ranging  from 93 to 105 percent  with the highest rsd being of 4.1  which is well within the limits for the  aoec recommendations  and also showed that this will work for  traditional chinese medicine as well as  spices and oats and corn  shown here are the hplc conditions for  aflatoxins we used an alliance  e2695 with a fluorescence detector that  had a photochemical reactor  we used a novapack c18 waters column  the column temp was 25 degrees c sample  temp was 25 degrees c the injection  volume was 50  microliters the flow was 0.8 mils a  minute  and the mobile phase was water methanol  5545 isocratic the software was waters  and power software for the system  the uplc conditions for aflatoxins are  detailed here  the lc system was a waters acuity uplc  h-class with fdn sample manager  the detection was an acuity fluorescence  detector with a large volume flow cell  excitation was 360 emission was 440.  the column that was used was a uplc  acuity hss t3 column  column temp was 25 degrees sample  temperature was 25 degrees c injection  volume was 3 to 6 microliters and the  flow rate was 0.3 mils a minute the  mobile phases were 55 45 water methanol  isocratic and the software that was used  for data reduction  was waters and power software  hplc and uplc chromatograms are shown  here  the one on the left hplc chromatogram  with the red and the green lines the red  line is unspiked black pepper and the  green line is spiked black pepper with  four ppb total aflatoxins and as you can  see there is no matrix interference in  the blank sample  the uplc chromatogram on the right  is from the analysis of an extract of  fallopia multiflora spiked with five  microgram per kilogram of total  aflatoxin  and shown below that is the aflatest  wbasr plus column  some of the advantages of the afla test  wbsr plus immunoaffinity column are  listed here  high performance  the aflatest wbsr plus method exceeds  aoac method performance requirements  giving  greater than 90 mean recovery of  aflatoxins b1 b2 g1 and g2  in both grains  corn wheat notes and difficult to  analyze food matrices such as chili  cocoa and traditional chinese medicine  the column and the method is  comprehensive  bicam's aflates wbsr plus immunoaffinity  column binds aflatoxin b1 b2 g1 and g2  as well as aflatoxin m1 m2 and stc  the method is flexible it's one  standardized method that is suitable for  a wide range of different commodities  it also has a wide testing range  aflatest wb sr plus can detect total  aflatoxin levels from  0.05  nanogram to 500 nanograms  with recoveries greater than 90 percent  the aflatest wb sr plus  method exceeds aoac method performance  requirements and shows that it is  capable of getting excellent recoveries  on both grains  and complex sample matrices  it is fast and easy  the uplc option provides an opportunity  to shorten the analytical runtime and  the use of a large flow cell in the  fluorescence detector  eliminates the need for post column  derivatization  and lastly we have overall performance  these methods have the desired  sensitivity selectivity  and overall performance that is  used to check compliance with regulatory  limits for aflatoxins  in a wide range of crops  and foods  what vicam delivers vicam delivers  testing options and programs to monitor  mycotoxins in a wide variety of  commodities  we are dedicated to ensure that our food  supply is mycotoxin free and safe for  human and animal consumption  i would like to thank you so very much  for joining me today  and for your interest in  the new technologies for complex  matrices and solving some of the  difficult challenges that occur when  analyzing difficult matrices  i hope that you have found this  particularly helpful  and that you will join us in the future  for other  topics  thank you so much

